WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.160
Erasmus is this year celebrating 30 years
of bringing people and cultures together.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.880
The programme started out in 1987

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.120
when just over 3 000 students from 11 EU countries
took part in the first exchanges.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.200
It has since grown to encompass
Vocational Education and Training,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.760
school education, adult education,
youth and sport,

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.040
giving nine million people the chance to have
a formative experience in 33 countries and beyond!

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.360
Erasmus Plus has also been instrumental
in paving the way for reform in education,

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.360
training and youth systems.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.880
Erasmus Plus has been proven to have
a hugely positive impact on participants.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.560
In Higher Education,

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:53.440
it doubles the chance of participants
being employed just a year after graduating.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.160
Whilst of those who undertake a traineeship abroad,

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.960
one in three is offered a job by their host company.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.120
Vocational Education and Training participants

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.760
find their first job faster and earn 25 percent
more than they would do otherwise.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.200
Voluntary experience abroad is considered
a plus by three-quarters of employers.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.560
But Erasmus Plus mobility
does not only help with job prospect.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.840
Erasmus Plus has been enriching lives
and opening minds for 30 years.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.040
Let’s now build together the future of Erasmus Plus!

